            {
                "entry_id": "0fac1d1d-5ab6-361e-8580-4d455a17365f",
                "word": "GoH",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "3dd3290c-c80f-471d-8bf1-ff5a42dddbbc",
                        "entry_id": "0fac1d1d-5ab6-361e-8580-4d455a17365f",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "GoHs"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e1f9efd3-c287-37f5-a2ae-f5e7d83f8838",
                        "entry_id": "0fac1d1d-5ab6-361e-8580-4d455a17365f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A person invited to attend a convention, in recognition of their contributions to the convention's field, to give one or more speeches and attend convention events."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "slang"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5ea7f37b-9031-4f99-a636-7dcad62fb624",
                                "sense_id": "e1f9efd3-c287-37f5-a2ae-f5e7d83f8838",
                                "text": "It will be readily seen that the GoH’s speech will be a convention highspot next Easter, and the Peterborough Committee are to be congratulated on an excellent choice."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1080f05f-243f-4a2d-b256-eb1668175c8a",
                                "sense_id": "e1f9efd3-c287-37f5-a2ae-f5e7d83f8838",
                                "text": "The same interviewing problem is bound to crop up again in the mail, which regularly brings requests for written replies to lengthy questionnaires. And it will certainly surface in April, when I'm scheduled to appear as GoH at the Cinecon in Australia. Far be it for me to complain about the trip; I feel it's my duty to go, if only to heal the breach in international relations caused by Tucker's visit some years ago. But there will be fan interviews and press interviews and -- if Tucker did as much damage as I suspect -- there may even be questions asked in Parliament."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1dabdf0f-1f95-401d-a72f-d71c0a823103",
                                "sense_id": "e1f9efd3-c287-37f5-a2ae-f5e7d83f8838",
                                "text": "Speaking for myself only, I have never been drawn to a con by the GoH, but I have often been introduced to the work of a writer as a result of their being Honoured by the con committee."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "c983fe68-b819-3aca-8735-d7b0a40170df",
                "word": "GOH",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "958bd1cb-0c71-48c4-8ea3-a1474350b097",
                        "entry_id": "c983fe68-b819-3aca-8735-d7b0a40170df",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "GOHs"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "838b9542-2ca2-3664-a5ab-9d8466d83425",
                        "entry_id": "c983fe68-b819-3aca-8735-d7b0a40170df",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Alternative letter-case form of GoH."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "alt-of",
                            "slang"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "26960ba3-3d67-4278-9953-4d27ca708e7f",
                                "sense_id": "838b9542-2ca2-3664-a5ab-9d8466d83425",
                                "text": "You need a popular/famous/realy^([sic]) talented artist/writer/actor/etc who is known for doing furry books/movies/art/etc for your GUEST OF HONOR. Some GOH posibilities^([sic]) for cons have to be asked up to two years before the con and some will only do cons if paid. They must be transported to the con and given rooms,food and such. Most cons do not pay bar tabs though. Two GOHs are a good idea in case one can't make it and cancels. Having back-ups is good to. It is posible^([sic]) to have a con without any famous GOHs, but it tends to hurt membership a bit."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "387420fc-805d-4a79-9b2c-2a50701e6ce1",
                                "sense_id": "838b9542-2ca2-3664-a5ab-9d8466d83425",
                                "text": "There used to be just one Pro GOH, and 90% of the time it was a writer. These days there's usually a Writer GOH, an Editor GOH, and an Artist GOH, and each will have an hour in which to make a speech. Check the schedule; usually they're at awkward times, as they're rarely big draws."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
